<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="53546" href="schedule/2017/fall/CMN/496/53546.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2017" href="schedule/2017.xml">2017</calendarYear><term id="120178" href="schedule/2017/fall.xml">Fall 2017</term><subject id="CMN" href="schedule/2017/fall/CMN.xml">Communication</subject><course id="496" href="schedule/2017/fall/CMN/496.xml">Adv Topics in Communication</course></parents><sectionNumber>JYG</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Intro Communication Analytics</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course covers basic skills of analyzing quantitative and qualitative data from the internet, social media, and survey. Students will learn basics of R programming and how to use R for data manipulation, statistical analysis, and data visualization. These skills provide an overview of communication analytics, and they also serve as a necessary foundation for students interested in learning advanced computational methods and data science in communication.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2017-08-28Z</startDate><endDate>2017-12-13Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="S4 ">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>09:30 AM</start><end>10:50 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>4007</roomNumber><buildingName>Lincoln Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Yang" firstName="J">Yang, J</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>